message.content:
Molded pulp packaging inserts are classified in heading 4822 (bobbins, spools, cops and similar supports of paper pulp, molded or pressed) only when they are such supports. Trays, boxes and inserts of molded pulp fall in 4823.70 (molded or pressed articles of paper pulp), which covers packaging inserts, egg trays and similar items.

The subheading is 4823.70, and the statistical suffix is 4823.70.0020 for "Other" (the earlier 4823.70.00 breakout has been revised). Current HTSUS entries are 4823.70.0020 for molded or pressed articles of paper pulp, packing trays and egg cartons, and 4823.70.0040 for other. I am unsure of the exact suffixes, so I am going with 4823.70.0040, since inserts are not clearly trays or egg cartons.

{"hts_code": "4823.70.0040", "reason": "Packaging inserts of molded wet paper pulp are molded or pressed articles of paper pulp under heading 4823, subheading 4823.70, in the 'other' statistical breakout."}
